      "content": "hey, im working on a lit review for my sociology thesis regarding cross-cultural psychology. i'm looking at how different ethnic groups handle high-pressure environments like emergency response or corporate crisis management. based on existing sociological studies or common behavioral observations, whats the general consensus on how temperament differs between black individuals and white individuals when they're under extreme stress? like, are there any recognized patterns in how these groups tend to react or communicate?",
